---
layout: base.njk
title: Skills
description: Agent skills from Ran Craycraft’s work, free to install in Claude, Codex, Cursor and other agents, so you can do it yourself or raise the bar on it.
permalink: /skills/
section: skills
---
<header class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-title serif">Skills</h1>
  <div class="grid">
    <p class="span-main lede serif">Some of what I write about can be handed to an AI agent as a skill. Install one to do it yourself, or improve on it and tell me what you changed. They’re free to use under the MIT License.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section grid list-section" aria-labelledby="skills-h">
  <h2 id="skills-h" class="rail eyebrow strong">Skills</h2>
  <ol class="span-main entries">
    {%- for key, sk in skills %}
    {%- set from = collections.posts | withSkill(key) %}
    <li><a href="{{ (from.url + '#skill-' + key) if from else ('/skills/' + key + '/SKILL.md') }}" class="entry">
      <span class="entry-title skill-name-sm">{{ sk.name }}</span>
      <span class="entry-desc">{{ sk.description }}</span>
      {%- if from %}<span class="meta">From {{ from.data.title }}</span>{% endif %}
    </a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>
